{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43788552",
      "title": "Defining Component Inputs",
      "lectureOrder": 31,
      "videoOrder": 27,
      "sourceHash": "b39dd510e0da8f51f75949218530e80deebc60ea01325e1679684e435d5702d1",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.51,
          "end": 2.97,
          "en": "To accept such inputs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.97,
          "end": 7.62,
          "en": "such settable properties on your components, you have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.62,
          "end": 10.62,
          "en": "to go to the component that should accept the input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.62,
          "end": 13.89,
          "en": "And then as a first step, add a property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.89,
          "end": 16.8,
          "en": "that should be settable from outside.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.8,
          "end": 19.56,
          "en": "For example, here we could say that we want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.56,
          "end": 24.56,
          "en": "to accept this avatar here, so this image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.17,
          "end": 28.11,
          "en": "of the user as an input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.11,
          "end": 31.32,
          "en": "And we do that by adding a property named avatar,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.32,
          "end": 34.83,
          "en": "for example, and by then decorating it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.83,
          "end": 37.14,
          "en": "with another decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.14,
          "end": 39.84,
          "en": "So decorators like this component decorator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.84,
          "end": 42.72,
          "en": "cannot just be added to classes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.72,
          "end": 46.173,
          "en": "but instead also to properties of classes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.37,
          "end": 49.65,
          "en": "And the decorator we need to add here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.65,
          "end": 53.04,
          "en": "to this property is the input decorator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.04,
          "end": 56.523,
          "en": "which is also imported from @Angular/core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.93,
          "end": 60.54,
          "en": "It's this input decorator that's added here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.54,
          "end": 63.36,
          "en": "and that's then also executed like a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.36,
          "end": 65.043,
          "en": "by adding parentheses here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.69,
          "end": 69.53999999999999,
          "en": "And this will mark this property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.53999999999999,
          "end": 72.66,
          "en": "as settable from outside.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.66,
          "end": 76.293,
          "en": "And I'll fix this error, which I have here in just a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 77.19,
          "end": 80.76,
          "en": "But with input added here, we can then go to the place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.76,
          "end": 84.15,
          "en": "where we use our component as an element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 84.15,
          "end": 88.053,
          "en": "and then there set this avatar property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 89.07,
          "end": 92.46000000000001,
          "en": "And we can use property binding here as well to set it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 92.46000000000001,
          "end": 94.56,
          "en": "to a dynamic value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 94.56,
          "end": 97.68,
          "en": "Now that of course, means that here in this case, we have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 97.68,
          "end": 101.07,
          "en": "to make sure that the app component has access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 101.07,
          "end": 102.78,
          "en": "to all the users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102.78,
          "end": 105.55,
          "en": "so that we can set them here in its template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 106.47,
          "end": 109.25999999999999,
          "en": "and therefore in the app component ts file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 109.25999999999999,
          "end": 113.46000000000001,
          "en": "we can start by importing the dummy users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 113.46000000000001,
          "end": 116.163,
          "en": "from this dummy users file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 117.66,
          "end": 120.81,
          "en": "And we can then add a property to the app component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 120.81,
          "end": 123.33,
          "en": "so that we can get access to that data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 123.33,
          "end": 126.75,
          "en": "from inside the template of this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 126.75,
          "end": 129.69,
          "en": "And that property could be called users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 129.69,
          "end": 132.993,
          "en": "and we set it equal to dummy users for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 134.85,
          "end": 137.94,
          "en": "This is how we can expose this import data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 137.94,
          "end": 140.133,
          "en": "in the template of this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 141.12,
          "end": 145.14,
          "en": "Now in the app component HTML file, we could set the avatar",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 145.14,
          "end": 149.37,
          "en": "of this first user here to users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 149.37,
          "end": 152.77,
          "en": "Then we can access the first user with index zero",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 153.63,
          "end": 156.66,
          "en": "and access the avatar property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 156.66,
          "end": 158.57999999999998,
          "en": "This is how we could set this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 158.57999999999998,
          "end": 163.05,
          "en": "And of course on the second user element here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 163.05,
          "end": 166.17000000000002,
          "en": "we could then access the second user by using an index",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 166.17000000000002,
          "end": 167.94299999999998,
          "en": "of one like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 169.71,
          "end": 172.98,
          "en": "And we will soon learn about a more efficient mechanism",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 172.98,
          "end": 177.12,
          "en": "for outputting multiple components based on some array data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 177.12,
          "end": 179.4,
          "en": "But for now, we can do it manually like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 179.4,
          "end": 182.163,
          "en": "for the first four users, let's say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 184.47,
          "end": 186.36,
          "en": "And now we of course still have an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 186.36,
          "end": 189.66,
          "en": "in the user component TypeScript file though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 189.66,
          "end": 194.28,
          "en": "the error is that the avatar member, so this property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 194.28,
          "end": 198.48,
          "en": "of this class implicitly has an any type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 198.48,
          "end": 201.06,
          "en": "and that's now a complaint by TypeScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 201.06,
          "end": 203.16,
          "en": "which we have to fix here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 203.16,
          "end": 206.7,
          "en": "And thus far we didn't have to deal with such complaints",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 206.7,
          "end": 211.14,
          "en": "because thus far we only worked with properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 211.14,
          "end": 216.14,
          "en": "or constants or variables that received an initial value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 216.93,
          "end": 219.63,
          "en": "But if you have a property like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 219.63,
          "end": 222.9,
          "en": "which at the moment doesn't have an initial value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 222.9,
          "end": 225.39,
          "en": "because we expect that value to be set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 225.39,
          "end": 229.59,
          "en": "from outside this component, TypeScript complains",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 229.59,
          "end": 231.66,
          "en": "that it doesn't know which type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 231.66,
          "end": 235.05,
          "en": "of value will eventually be received here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 235.05,
          "end": 238.17000000000002,
          "en": "And it's kind of TypeScript's main thing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 238.17000000000002,
          "end": 241.95,
          "en": "to know which kind of value is being used where,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 241.95,
          "end": 243.723,
          "en": "that's why it's complaining here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 244.98,
          "end": 249.72,
          "en": "Therefore, what we should do here is explicitly assign",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 249.72,
          "end": 252.51,
          "en": "a value type to this property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 252.51,
          "end": 256.68,
          "en": "By adding a colon here, that's a special TypeScript feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 256.68,
          "end": 260.97,
          "en": "that you can assign a type to a property, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 260.97,
          "end": 263.65,
          "en": "by adding a colon after the property name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 264.75,
          "end": 268.29,
          "en": "and by then setting the type that will be received here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 268.29,
          "end": 270.363,
          "en": "And in this case, this will be a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 271.41,
          "end": 273.06,
          "en": "and that's now one of the types",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 273.06,
          "end": 274.947,
          "en": "that are built into TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 274.947,
          "end": 278.15999999999997,
          "en": "and that are supported out of the box.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 278.15999999999997,
          "end": 281.88,
          "en": "You have string, number, Boolean,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 281.88,
          "end": 285.27,
          "en": "and you can also set up more complex object types",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 285.27,
          "end": 289.08,
          "en": "for example, though, we'll take a look at that later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 289.08,
          "end": 291.63,
          "en": "For the moment, we can just use a string here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 291.63,
          "end": 294,
          "en": "because the avatar will be a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 294,
          "end": 296.90999999999997,
          "en": "and we now get a different error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 296.90999999999997,
          "end": 301.53,
          "en": "We get a error that the property avatar has no initializer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 301.53,
          "end": 304.293,
          "en": "and is not definitely assigned in the constructor,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 305.46,
          "end": 309.48,
          "en": "which in the end means that TypeScript now knows",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 309.48,
          "end": 311.22,
          "en": "that this should be a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 311.22,
          "end": 312.93,
          "en": "but it does not understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 312.93,
          "end": 315.45,
          "en": "that we're using an Angular mechanism",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 315.45,
          "end": 318.63,
          "en": "for receiving the value of this property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 318.63,
          "end": 320.22,
          "en": "All TypeScript sees",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 320.22,
          "end": 324.24,
          "en": "is that there is no value being set at any point",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 324.24,
          "end": 325.38,
          "en": "in this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 325.38,
          "end": 328.62,
          "en": "Instead, it's an uninitialized property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 328.62,
          "end": 331.473,
          "en": "And that's exactly what this complaint is about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 332.82,
          "end": 336.6,
          "en": "Now, we can work around that by adding an exclamation mark",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 336.6,
          "end": 338.31,
          "en": "after the property name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 338.31,
          "end": 340.89,
          "en": "That's another TypeScript feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 340.89,
          "end": 344.7,
          "en": "which simply tells TypeScript that we know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 344.7,
          "end": 348.57,
          "en": "that this will definitely be set to some value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 348.57,
          "end": 352.17,
          "en": "even though TypeScript can't see it in this code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 352.17,
          "end": 355.659,
          "en": "But of course, we know that the value will be set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 355.659,
          "end": 359.07,
          "en": "from outside here by assigning an avatar value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 359.07,
          "end": 361.503,
          "en": "when we use the user component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 362.61,
          "end": 366.6,
          "en": "And that's now how we can get this avatar property value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 366.6,
          "end": 368.52,
          "en": "from outside this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 368.52,
          "end": 372.723,
          "en": "and how we can therefore reuse this app user component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 374.16,
          "end": 376.98,
          "en": "Now of course, we can add more inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 376.98,
          "end": 379.2,
          "en": "and also add an input for the name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 379.2,
          "end": 380.94,
          "en": "which will also be a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 380.94,
          "end": 383.28,
          "en": "so that we can also set the user name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 383.28,
          "end": 385.773,
          "en": "from outside the user component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 387.42,
          "end": 388.74,
          "en": "Therefore in the app component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 388.74,
          "end": 390.73,
          "en": "we can now also set the name here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 391.86,
          "end": 394.68,
          "en": "and also use property binding there to set it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 394.68,
          "end": 396.81,
          "en": "to a dynamic value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 396.81,
          "end": 401.313,
          "en": "and set the name to users[0].name in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 402.3,
          "end": 405.51,
          "en": "and then repeat this for all the instances",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 405.51,
          "end": 407.28,
          "en": "of this user component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 407.28,
          "end": 410.673,
          "en": "just with different indexes like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 412.89,
          "end": 415.40999999999997,
          "en": "And now there's just one last step,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 415.40999999999997,
          "end": 417.81,
          "en": "and that is that we should bring back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 417.81,
          "end": 420.213,
          "en": "this computed image path here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 421.14,
          "end": 424.77,
          "en": "Using a getter again, since I'm not using a signal here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 424.77,
          "end": 428.16,
          "en": "because I'm relying on that image path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 428.16,
          "end": 429.93,
          "en": "in that template, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 429.93,
          "end": 430.983,
          "en": "I'm using it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 432.6,
          "end": 437.6,
          "en": "So we should actually again, return that image path here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 438.24,
          "end": 441.51,
